ich is the highest number of steps such that its sampling time is within that of the baseline 25-step DDIM. Here LTSP2 and STSP2 are Lie-Trotter and Strang splitting methods with the combination [PLMS2, PLMS1]. In Table 2, we report the results of three different ImageNet resolutions and the average sampling time per image in seconds.\nOur STSP4 performs best on all measurements except Recall on ImageNet512. On ImageNet512, PLMS4 has the highest Recall score but a poor FID of 16, indicating that the generated images have good distribution coverage but may poorly represent the real distribution. On ImageNet256, STSP4 can yield 4.49 FID in 20 steps, compared to 4.59 FID in 250 steps originally reported in the paper (Dhariwal & Nichol, 2021); our STSP4 is about 9.4\u00d7 faster when tested on the same machine."
